Observation: Many goal predicates are similar to initial but for other entities.

We have shift_candidate_alpha already finalized, prepared, vehicle_allocated, task_profile_linked, transport_leg_linked, compliance linked, compliance_validation_complete, constraint_applied, operator_alignment_confirmed, dispatch_ready. However goal wants dispatch_allocated, dispatched for shift_candidate_alpha as well. So we need to allocate dispatch slot and execute dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha.

Similarly for origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha we need to prepare, allocate vehicle, lock availability, confirm, load payload, assemble transport leg, etc.

Shift_candidate_beta needs many things: prepared, vehicle_allocated (to vehicle_unit_gamma), task_profile_linked, loading_container linked already, loading_container loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, staged for loading, loading_verified, clearance_established, skill_certificate linked, compliance_certificate linked, operator linked, dispatch_slot linked, dispatch_allocated, dispatched, finalized, etc.

Also need origin and destination availability prepared, vehicle allocated, origin_node_ready/occupied etc.

We need to produce a plan achieving all these. Likely we need to follow a sequence: create candidates (already created), prepare candidates, allocate vehicles, link task profiles, confirm preparedness, activate nodes, lock availabilities, confirm availability, load payloads, assemble transport leg, load container onto leg, stage candidate, verify loading, establish clearance, link service window, validate route, finalize candidate, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.

Given many entities, we need to do for origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha, shift_candidate_alpha, shift_candidate_beta.

But note many actions are parameterized with candidate being schedule_candidate type (like shift_candidate). For origin/destination availability they are also candidate_entity type (origin_candidate_availability etc) and can use similar actions like allocate_vehicle_unit, attach_task_profile, confirm_candidate_preparedness, etc. Actually many actions apply to candidate_entity generic type; they have precondition candidate_created ?candidate and maybe vehicle_allocated etc. So we can treat origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha as candidates for many actions.

We need to check each action's parameter types.

List of actions relevant:

- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate (?candidate - candidate_entity ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Preconditions: dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate.
Effect: dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.

- allocate_vehicle_unit (?candidate - candidate_entity ?vehicle_unit - vehicle_unit)
Pre: candidate_created ?candidate, not vehicle_allocated ?candidate, vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit.
Effect: vehicle_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, not vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit.

- attach_task_profile (?candidate - candidate_entity ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Pre: candidate_created ?candidate, vehicle_allocated ?candidate, route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile.
Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile.

- confirm_candidate_preparedness (?candidate - candidate_entity ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Pre: candidate_created ?candidate, vehicle_allocated ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not candidate_prepared ?candidate.
Effect: candidate_prepared ?candidate.

- load_origin_payload (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?payload_unit - cargo_payload)
Pre: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, cargo_available ?payload_unit, not origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability.
Effect: origin_node_occupied ?origin_node, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, origin_payload_linked ?origin_availability ?payload_unit, not cargo_available ?payload_unit.

- unload_origin_payload (similar but need candidate_task_profile_linked etc)

- load_destination_payload similar.

- activate_origin_node (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Pre: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, not origin_node_ready ?origin_node, not origin_node_occupied ?origin_node.
Effect: origin_node_ready ?origin_node.

- lock_origin_availability (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?operator_resource - operator_resource)
Pre: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, origin_node_ready ?origin_node, not origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability.
Effect: origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability.

Similarly for destination.

- assign_operator_resource (?candidate - candidate_entity ?operator_resource - operator_resource)
Pre: candidate_prepared ?candidate, operator_available ?operator_resource.
Effect: candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource, not operator_available ?operator_resource.

- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate as above.

- execute_schedule_dispatch (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?vehicle_unit - vehicle_unit ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot)
Pre: dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?candidate.
Effect: dispatched ?candidate, vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot.

- execute_origin_dispatch similar but for origin_availability.

- execute_destination_dispatch similar.

- assemble_transport_leg (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?destination_node - destination_node ?transport_leg - transport_leg)
Pre: origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability, origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node, destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node, origin_node_ready ?origin_node, destination_node_ready ?destination_node, origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability, destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability, transport_leg_available ?transport_leg.
Effect: transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, transport_leg_origin_linked ?transport_leg ?origin_node, transport_leg_destination_linked ?transport_leg ?destination_node, not transport_leg_available ?transport_leg.

- authorize_transport_leg_loading (?transport_leg - transport_leg ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Pre: transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg.
Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg.

