- establish_clearance_nominal (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?compliance_certificate - compliance_certificate ?loading_container - loading_container ?transport_leg - transport_leg)
Pre: candidate_loading_verified ?candidate, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_clearance_established ?candidate.
Effect: candidate_clearance_established ?candidate.

- establish_clearance_origin_loaded requires origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded.

- establish_clearance_destination_loaded requires destination_leg_loaded, not origin_leg_loaded.

- establish_clearance_full_load requires both origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded.

- attach_service_window (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?service_window - service_window)
Pre: candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, service_window_available ?service_window.
Effect: candidate_service_window_linked ?candidate ?service_window, not service_window_available ?service_window.

- validate_route_sequence (?candidate - schedule_candidate ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile ?service_window - service_window)
Pre: candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, candidate_service_window_linked ?candidate ?service_window, candidate_origin_availability_linked ?candidate ?origin_availability, candidate_destination_availability_linked ?candidate ?destination_availability, origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability, destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not route_sequence_validated ?candidate.
Effect: route_sequence_validated ?candidate.

- finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (?candidate - schedule_candidate)
Pre: candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, route_sequence_validated ?candidate, not candidate_finalized ?candidate.
Effect: candidate_finalized ?candidate, dispatch_ready ?candidate.

- finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation similar.

- finalize_candidate_direct (?candidate - schedule_candidate)
Pre: candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, not candidate_finalized ?candidate.
Effect: candidate_finalized ?candidate, dispatch_ready ?candidate.

We also have actions to detach_task_profile, release_operator, release_skill, release_compliance, etc but likely not needed.

Goal includes many dispatch_allocated and dispatched for all four candidates (origin, destination, shift_alpha, shift_beta). Also wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_unit_gamma after dispatch (they become available after dispatch). Initially vehicle_unit_beta is available; after dispatch of shift_candidate_alpha (vehicle_unit_gamma) and destination_availability_alpha (vehicle_unit_beta) etc, they become available.

Goal also wants vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha and shift_candidate_beta (both to vehicle_unit_beta and vehicle_unit_gamma respectively). Actually goal: candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta and candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma. Also vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha and shift_candidate_beta. So after allocating vehicle, they become allocated and vehicle not available.

Goal wants vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha and vehicle_unit_gamma after dispatch (since after dispatch, vehicle becomes available). Initially vehicle_unit_alpha not available; after we allocate it to someone and then dispatch, it becomes available. Similarly vehicle_unit_gamma initially not available; after allocate to shift_candidate_beta and dispatch, becomes available.

Goal also wants origin_node_occupied and origin_node_ready; destination_node_occupied and destination_node_ready.

